in moving out on the other hand  the russians want to make the point that  while they're willing to agree to allow  ukraine to transport grain they're not  going to slow down their attack on other  sorts of targets including targets in  port cities like odessa  and so what it suggests is that the  future of the war will be quite complex  with some areas of agreement whether  grain  or pow exchanges moving ahead  at the same time  you know continuing hostilities  occur  good talking to you that's very clear  thanks for joining us uh michael desch  professor of international relations at  the university of notre dame  my pleasure  you

